meta {
  name: GetMultipleCandidates
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/npp/artikelscan?scan={{nppScanMultiBarcode}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq multiple
  res.body.article: isNull
  res.body.empty: eq true
  res.body.candidates: isArray
}

docs {
  GET /web/npp/artikelscan?scan=<barcode> - step 3 of
  Luna.BusinessLogic.NPPArtikelScanBE:ResolveScan where the barcode/
  subcode search (artikel-x04 + art-subcodes-x1, deduplicated by artnr)
  finds 2+ distinct artnr candidates -> NOT an error, 200 with "status":
  "multiple", "article": null, "empty": true, and a "candidates" array
  (each {artnr, omschrijving}).

  {{nppScanMultiBarcode}} must be set (collection/environment variable,
  not currently in Local.bru) to a real barcode/subcode value from
  LunaNew that maps to 2+ distinct artnr values - likely rare/synthetic
  data, may need to be seeded for this test to actually exercise the
  "multiple" branch.

  Read-only - backed by Backend/src/Luna/Web/NPPArtikelScanHandler.cls +
  Luna/BusinessLogic/NPPArtikelScanBE.cls.
}
